window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-6fe4dfe996bacf5b"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"run-verified-operations\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">运行经过核验的运营工作流</h1> <p>运行可重复的工作流，并核验结果。</p> <p>使用 ChatGPT 规范化输入、运行获准的脚本或 API、对有限范围内的失败进行重试，并根据日志或成果核验结果后再汇报。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>输入结构化、需要明确授权且结果应可审计的运营任务。</li> <li>需要重复运行的工作流，例如权限更新、批量邀请、配额调整、客户设置、路由检查和迁移跟进。</li> <li>希望 ChatGPT 在明确范围内执行任务，并准确报告成功、失败或需要人工决策事项的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">起步提示词</h2> <p>运行获准的工作流</p> <p>建议模型：<code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> · 建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">我需要运行以下工作流：\n\n目标：[what should happen]\n输入：[CSV, Google Sheet, list, ticket, or file path]\n授权或政策来源：[Slack thread, doc, ticket, or none]\n执行工具：[script, API, CLI, skill, or manual app workflow]\n核验成果：[result CSV, log, dashboard, screenshot, or other proof]\n\n请执行以下事项：\n- 检查输入；只询问缺少的必填字段\n- 运行工作流前规范化日期、金额、负责人和 ID\n- 如果工作流支持试运行，先运行试运行\n- 只执行获准的范围\n- 为每个项目记录一行成功或失败结果\n- 对瞬时故障重试一次；不要重新运行已成功的项目\n- 汇总总数、失败项、重试次数和核验成果\n\n遇到不可逆操作或范围变更时暂停。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">定时任务</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">智能体技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可查看该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"run-operations-you-can-audit\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">运行可审计的运营任务</h2> <p>如果你需要定期执行可重复的运营任务，例如为用户授予访问权限、应用批量更新，或使用不同参数多次运行脚本，可以让 ChatGPT 自动化执行，并提供可审计的输出。</p> <p>当你希望 ChatGPT 运行一项可重复操作，并提供可供你或团队成员检查的核验成果时，可使用此工作流。</p> <p><a id=\"describe-the-task-and-inputs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">描述任务和输入</h2> <ol> <li>提供要批量处理的输入表、文件、工单或其它清单。</li> <li>如果有规定允许范围的授权来源或政策，请提供给它。</li> <li>告诉 ChatGPT 要使用哪个脚本、API、技能、CLI 或应用工作流。</li> <li>如果工作流支持试运行，可以先要求试运行。</li> <li>请它运行批量操作，并为每项记录一行成功或失败结果。</li> </ol> <p>保持范围明确，并要求 ChatGPT 只有在具备所有必需输入时才运行操作。 如果某一行缺少必填字段，应标记该行，而不是猜测。</p> <p>通过 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件（本地尚未收录）</a> 连接执行操作所需的工具，例如工单系统，或包含待处理项目的电子表格。</p> <p><a id=\"require-proof-to-verify-the-result\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">要求提供核验结果的证据</h2> <p>有用的运营执行应包含你或团队成员可以检查的结果，例如 CSV、日志文件、仪表盘链接、截图、PR 检查结果或其它证明。在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，运行完成后，你可以<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/artifacts-viewer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开并检查生成的文件（本地尚未收录）</a>来核验结果。</p> <p><a id=\"turn-the-run-into-a-reusable-workflow\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">将运行流程变成可复用的工作流</h2> <p>首次运行成功后，请 ChatGPT 记录可重复使用的部分。常见工作流可以整理成<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">技能（本地尚未收录）</a>或<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">定时任务（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Turn this operations run into a [reusable ChatGPT skill/scheduled task].\n\nCapture:\n\n- required inputs\n- approval or policy source\n- runner command, API, skill, or app workflow\n- dry-run behavior if applicable\n- verification artifact\n- retry policy\n- final report format\n\nKeep the operation narrow and pause before irreversible actions.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请将这次运维执行整理成 [reusable ChatGPT skill/scheduled task]。\n\n记录：\n\n- 必需的输入\n- 审批或政策依据\n- 执行命令、API、技能或应用工作流\n- 适用时的预演行为\n- 验证产物\n- 重试策略\n- 最终报告格式\n\n严格限制操作范围，并在不可逆操作之前暂停。</div></div> <p>对于定时运营任务，只有在手动运行已产生可靠结果后，才创建定时任务。可能永久影响访问权限或数据的敏感操作，应继续保持为草稿，除非你明确希望 ChatGPT 执行。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"run-verified-operations\">Run verified operations</h1> <p>Run repeatable workflows and verify the result.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT to normalize inputs, run approved scripts or APIs, retry bounded failures, and verify the result from logs or artifacts before reporting back.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Operations tasks with structured inputs, explicit approval, and a result that should be auditable.</li> <li>Repeated workflows such as access updates, invite batches, quota changes, customer setup tasks, routing checks, and migration follow-ups.</li> <li>Teams that need ChatGPT to run a narrow scope and report exactly what succeeded, failed, or needs a human decision.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Run an Approved Workflow</p> <p>Suggested model：<code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> · Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">I need to run this workflow:\n\nGoal: [what should happen]\nInputs: [CSV, Google Sheet, list, ticket, or file path]\nApproval or policy source: [Slack thread, doc, ticket, or none]\nRunner: [script, API, CLI, skill, or manual app workflow]\nVerification artifact: [result CSV, log, dashboard, screenshot, or other proof]\n\nPlease:\n- inspect the inputs and ask only for missing required fields\n- normalize dates, amounts, owners, and IDs before running the workflow\n- run a dry run first when the workflow supports it\n- run only the approved scope\n- record one success or failure row per item\n- retry transient failures once without restarting successful rows\n- summarize totals, failures, retries, and verification artifacts\n\nPause before irreversible actions or scope changes.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">Scheduled tasks</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"run-operations-you-can-audit\">Run operations you can audit</h2> <p>If you have repeatable operations you need to run regularly, such as giving access to a user, applying a batch update, or calling a script with different parameters for example, you can use ChatGPT to automate it and give you an auditable output.</p> <p>Use this workflow when ChatGPT should run a repeatable operation and show you what happened with an artifact that counts as verification.</p> <h2 id=\"describe-the-task-and-inputs\">Describe the task and inputs</h2> <ol> <li>Give ChatGPT the input table, files, tickets, or other list it should batch run the process on.</li> <li>Point it to the approval source or policy that defines the allowed scope, if applicable.</li> <li>Tell ChatGPT which script, API, skill, CLI, or app workflow should do the work.</li> <li>Optionally, ask for a dry run when the workflow supports one.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to run the batch operation and record one success or failure row per item.</li> </ol> <p>Keep the scope narrow, and add instructions for ChatGPT to run the operation only when it has all the required inputs. If a row is missing a required field, ChatGPT should flag that row instead of guessing.</p> <p>Connect the tools you use to run the operation with <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">plugins (not in this local snapshot)</a>, for example your ticketing system or your spreadsheet with list items.</p> <h2 id=\"require-proof-to-verify-the-result\">Require proof to verify the result</h2> <p>A useful operations run includes a result that you or a teammate can inspect, such as a CSV, log file, dashboard link, screenshot, PR check, or other proof that the operation was successful. In the ChatGPT desktop app, you can <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/artifacts-viewer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">open and inspect generated files (not in this local snapshot)</a> after the run to verify the result.</p> <h2 id=\"turn-the-run-into-a-reusable-workflow\">Turn the run into a reusable workflow</h2> <p>After the first successful run, ask ChatGPT to capture the repeatable parts. For common workflows, this can become a <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">skill (not in this local snapshot)</a> or a <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">scheduled task (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Turn this operations run into a [reusable ChatGPT skill/scheduled task].\n\nCapture:\n\n- required inputs\n- approval or policy source\n- runner command, API, skill, or app workflow\n- dry-run behavior if applicable\n- verification artifact\n- retry policy\n- final report format\n\nKeep the operation narrow and pause before irreversible actions.\n</code></pre> <p>For scheduled operations, create a scheduled task only after the manual run produces reliable output. Keep sensitive actions that might affect access or data permanently draft-only unless you explicitly want ChatGPT to take them.</p>"};
